0047: 
0048:     Rule:
0049:     - Rotate the entire input grid 90 degrees counterclockwise.
0050:     - Create a blue one-pixel frame around two vertical copies of the rotated grid.
0051:     - Use the input background color for the two endpoints of every horizontal frame/separator row.
0052: 
0053:     Key insight: The output is not a crop of the foreground objects; it is two copies of the complete rotated input, separated and enclosed by a newly added blue border.
0054:     """
